  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NOTHING_TO_AUDIT` | No completed Round / no committed code to compare |
    | `H_SPEC_MISSING` | The spec the ticket references does not exist |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_1_MECHANICAL">
      <Goal>Get the mechanical findings from the tool. Take them as given.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run `sdd-check --task <ticket-path>` (and `--all` for an epic, per `AX_AUDIT_MODES`) per `AX_MECHANICAL_VIA_SDD_CHECK`
        — it reports the deterministic findings: structure / anchors / Task-ID + Status, fabricated-DONE,
        the phase graph, Execution-Log completeness, the task DAG, and tracker↔ticket coherence. Take these
        as given — the tool owns them. Then INDEPENDENTLY re-run the green gate — `sdd-verify --profile full`,
        `gennady lint --spec=<module-spec>` (cast + closed-world inventory over the changed files), and
        `gennady testcov --run --min=80` (coverage gate — project line coverage ≥ 80% at task completion):
        Always re-derive the gate yourself rather than trust the worker's logged `ver` lines; a gate that fails
        here, a `ver` logged for a command that does not actually pass, or coverage below the gate, is a `BLOCKER`.
        When the audit closes a WHOLE module
        (its last task — every sibling DONE), add the reverse closed-world sweep over the module's code root:
        `gennady lint --spec=<module-spec> --inventory-reverse <module-code-dir>` — every entity declared in the
        inventory must now be exported by some file (`ERR_CLI_LINT_INVENTORY_UNIMPLEMENTED` = declared-but-unbuilt
        / renamed-away). Run it only at module close; for a single mid-module phase the per-phase diff is a subset
        and would false-positive. BDD↔test substance, rules-cascade resolution, and
        stale-after-pivot belong to STEP_2 (semantic), not the tool.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_SEMANTIC">
      <Goal>Add the layer the tool cannot — meaning.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read the artifacts (per `AX_READ_PER_MANIFEST` — the bounded artifacts list + relevant spec
        anchors, not the whole repo) and the git diff (`AX_AUDIT_READS_CODE`, `AX_GIT_DIFF_SCAN`).
        Run the closed-world inventory sweep FIRST (`AX_CLOSED_WORLD_PRIMARY_CHECK`):
        1. collect declared entities from `specs/<scope>/<module>/<module>.spec.md` 2 Entity Inventory;
        2. enumerate entities the code actually exposes — classes, interfaces, exported types/functions
           with public surface;
        3. collect the `intro <X> ← <Y>` lines phase agents logged in the Execution Log;
        4. flag every code entity outside inventory ∪ logged-introductions as `CLOSED_WORLD_DRIFT`
           (`BLOCKER`).
        Verify each phase's `Rules:` list against what the cascade would derive now, including the
        transitive `<DependsOn>` closure (`AX_RULES_CASCADE_VERIFICATION`). Then judge
        what is irreducibly semantic: does the implementation satisfy the contract's postconditions /
        invariants in substance; is a `real-runtime` claim actually backed or a stub
        (`AX_RUNTIME_BACKING_VERIFICATION`); capture spec gaps as insights
        (`AX_INSIGHT_BACKFLOW_CAPTURE`). Classify each per `AX_DRIFT_TAXONOMY`, severity per `AX_SEVERITY_TAGGING`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_ROUTE">
      <Goal>Route findings; summarize. Route only — leave the fix to its owner.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Emit each finding as a neutral proposal (`AX_FINDINGS_AS_PROPOSALS`, `AX_NEUTRAL_FINDINGS`,
        `FINDING_FORMAT`) routed to its home (`AX_FINDING_ROUTING`: phase-fix / ticket-update / spec-edit
        / decision-log); route only, MUST leave the fix to its owner (`AX_NO_AUTO_FIX`). Present the ephemeral chat summary
        (`AX_EPHEMERAL_OUTPUT`, `AUDIT_SESSION_SUMMARY_FORMAT`). If the round triggers a reopen, append an
        Audit Rounds section to the ticket (`AX_REOPEN_ROUNDS_IN_TICKET`) —
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/audit-round.xml")` for the format. Return the
        verdict (PASS / PASS_WITH_ACKNOWLEDGED_RISKS / FAIL + `phases_to_fix`) to the orchestrator.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <OutputContracts>
    {{> "contract/audit/finding-format"}}

